def H(code, d, q, right, wrong, e): return B.hand(code, d, q, right, wrong, e)

# ---- 813 Robotics and Automation / Computer-Integrated Manufacturing I ----
H("813.d.1.A",3,"A student draws a 3D model of a motor mount on screen, adds dimensions and exports the drawing so the shop can make it. She is using:","computer-aided design (CAD) software to complete a design",["a spreadsheet to type a letter","a game console to play","a calculator to add"],"CAD creates digital designs.")
H("813.d.1.A",4,"One advantage of designing a part in CAD instead of by hand is that the design can be:","edited, measured and shared digitally with accuracy",["only printed once","drawn only in pencil","used only by its author"],"Digital designs are editable and shareable.")
H("813.d.1.B",3,"Before building a bracket, a team applies a simulated load to its CAD model and sees a red zone where stress is highest. They are analyzing:","the results of product testing in a simulated modeling environment",["a weather map","a sports table","a bank statement"],"Simulation shows weak points.")
H("813.d.1.B",4,"The main benefit of simulated testing before fabrication is that it:","finds design weaknesses without wasting material",["adds to material cost","skips design","needs no software"],"Cheaper than breaking prototypes.")
H("813.d.1.C",3,"After approving a gear design, a student cuts and assembles a working model on a 3D printer and a mill to see whether it meshes. She is fabricating:","a prototype of a mechanical part",["a final advertisement","a cafeteria tray","a classroom poster"],"Prototypes test designs.")
H("813.d.1.C",4,"A prototype is built mainly to:","test and improve a design before mass production",["replace all drawings","avoid planning","be sold unchanged"],"Prototypes reveal flaws early.")
H("813.d.2.A",3,"A class uses software to simulate how robots, conveyors and machines move parts through a small plant before building the line. They are using:","computer-integrated manufacturing techniques to simulate a manufacturing process",["a cooking show","a drawing contest","a voting booth"],"CIM links computers and machines.")
H("813.d.2.A",4,"Computer-integrated manufacturing links design, machines and data so that:","information flows automatically between steps",["every step is separate","workers copy numbers by hand","no records are kept"],"CIM integrates operations.")
H("813.d.2.B",3,"A conveyor stops unexpectedly, and a technician uses a laptop connected to the controller to see which input never turned on. He is:","troubleshooting programmable logic devices",["decorating the plant","shipping boxes","ordering lunch"],"PLC troubleshooting finds faults.")
H("813.d.2.B",4,"A PLC, or programmable logic controller, is used to:","automate machines based on programmed logic and sensor inputs",["compose music","cook food","print photos only"],"PLCs control equipment.")
H("813.d.3.A",3,"A student compares limit switches, proximity sensors and relays to decide which would detect a box arriving on a conveyor. She is:","researching the use of control devices",["researching paint colors","researching school menus","researching bus routes"],"Control devices sense and switch.")
H("813.d.3.A",4,"A sensor that detects an object without touching it is a:","proximity sensor",["manual lever","paintbrush","ruler"],"Proximity sensors detect near objects.")
H("813.d.3.B",3,"A team wires a push button, a relay and a lamp so pressing the button turns the lamp on and keeps it latched until a stop button is pressed. They are:","demonstrating the use of control devices",["avoiding wiring","writing a poem","drawing a map"],"Hands-on control circuits.")
H("813.d.3.B",4,"In a simple control circuit, a stop button is commonly wired to:","break the circuit and turn the device off",["add power","bypass the relay","increase voltage"],"Stop interrupts the circuit.")
H("813.d.4.A",3,"A student sketches a simple cylinder in CAM software and sets cutting tools, speeds and feeds for a lathe. She is designing a product using:","computer-aided manufacturing software for production on a CNC lathe",["a video editor","a spreadsheet only","a drawing pad only"],"CAM prepares machine instructions.")
H("813.d.4.A",4,"A CNC lathe is best suited to making parts that are:","round, such as shafts and pins",["flat sheets only","thin fabrics","liquid"],"Lathes spin round parts.")
H("813.d.4.B",3,"Before cutting metal, a student runs the lathe program in a simulator to check that the tool path clears the chuck. She is producing a product on:","a CNC lathe or a simulation",["a loom","a blender","a printer"],"Simulation previews cutting.")
H("813.d.4.B",4,"Why run a lathe program in a simulator first?","to find tool path errors before cutting real material",["to waste time","to avoid safety rules","to make parts bigger"],"Simulate before cutting.")
H("813.d.4.C",3,"A team draws a pocket and a hole pattern in CAM software and generates toolpaths for a milling machine. They are designing a product for production on:","a CNC mill",["a CNC lathe only","a sewing machine","a kiln"],"Mills cut pockets and holes.")
H("813.d.4.C",4,"A CNC mill typically moves a rotating cutter along:","several axes to remove material from a block",["no axes","one fixed line only","the ceiling"],"Mills use multi-axis motion.")
H("813.d.4.D",3,"After checking the simulation, a student clamps an aluminum block, loads the program and cuts a nameplate on the mill. She is producing a product on:","a CNC mill or a simulation",["a sewing table","a potter's wheel","a loom"],"Run the program on the mill.")
H("813.d.4.D",4,"Before starting a CNC mill program on a real part, the operator should always:","verify the work offset and tool setup",["remove the guard","skip the simulation","turn off the stop button"],"Verify setup.")
H("813.d.4.E",3,"Each team keeps a log of the plan, the run, the inspection results and the corrective changes for every project in a standard form. They are completing:","data sheets for plan, do, check and act forms and projects",["menus","playlists","grocery lists"],"PDCA documents improvement.")
H("813.d.4.E",4,"In the plan-do-check-act cycle, the 'check' step is where a team:","measures results against the plan",["ignores the data","starts a new product","ships boxes"],"Check = compare to plan.")
H("813.d.5.A",3,"Students build a small lever, a gear train and a pulley and demonstrate how each changes force or speed. They are identifying, describing and demonstrating:","mechanical devices",["fluid pumps only","electronic chips","weather tools"],"Mechanical devices transmit motion.")
H("813.d.5.A",4,"A gear train with a small gear driving a large gear will:","reduce speed and increase torque",["increase speed and reduce torque","change nothing","stop the shaft"],"Gearing trades speed for torque.")
H("813.d.5.B",3,"A class uses a hand pump, tubing and a small cylinder filled with fluid to lift a load and explains why the fluid transmits force. They are demonstrating:","fluid devices",["optical devices","wooden devices","magnetic toys"],"Fluids transmit pressure.")
H("813.d.5.B",4,"A hydraulic jack works because a liquid in a closed system:","transmits pressure equally in all directions",["compresses easily","disappears","stops all force"],"Pascal's principle.")
H("813.d.6.A",3,"A student labels a battery, a switch, a resistor and a motor on a schematic and describes what each does. She is identifying and describing:","electrical devices",["fluid devices","mechanical levers only","optical devices only"],"Electrical devices form circuits.")
H("813.d.6.A",4,"On a shop-floor wiring diagram, a technician sees a symbol for a device that can break the path so current stops flowing to a motor. That device is a:","switch",["capacitor","battery","resistor"],"A switch opens or closes the circuit path.")
H("813.d.6.B",3,"A team wires a motor to a battery through a switch, then adds a fuse and tests the circuit with a multimeter. They are demonstrating the use of:","electrical devices",["fluid devices","gear trains only","cooking tools"],"Hands-on circuits.")
H("813.d.6.B",4,"A multimeter set to volts is used to measure:","the electrical potential across two points",["the weight of a part","the length of a wire","the temperature of a room"],"Volts measure potential difference.")
H("813.d.6.C",3,"A class tests how a plastic part warps when baked at different temperatures and records its length each time. They are researching:","the effects of heat energy and temperature on products",["the effects of music on mood","the effects of lighting on color only","the effects of weather on traffic"],"Heat changes materials.")
H("813.d.6.C",4,"Most plastics will soften when:","heated above their rated temperature",["cooled slightly","painted","labeled"],"Thermal limits.")
H("813.d.7.A",3,"A quality technician learns that a certification from the International Organization for Standardization shows a plant follows agreed procedures for quality. She is researching:","industrial standards such as ISO",["pop standards","clothing sizes","sports rules"],"ISO standards promote consistency.")
H("813.d.7.A",4,"ISO standards help manufacturers by:","providing agreed quality and safety practices",["making products identical in color","reducing all costs","removing inspection"],"Common standards.")
H("813.d.7.B",3,"A chart sorts defect types from most to least frequent so the team can see that three causes produce most of the problems. This is a:","Pareto chart",["pie of cookies","map of roads","calendar"],"Pareto shows the vital few.")
H("813.d.7.B",4,"A Pareto chart is most useful for:","focusing on the few causes that create most defects",["listing every employee","drawing parts","selecting colors"],"80/20 rule.")
H("813.d.7.C",3,"A team plots the diameter of every fifth part on a control chart with upper and lower limits to see when the process drifts. They are applying:","statistical process control",["guesswork","gossip","random picks"],"SPC monitors stability.")
H("813.d.7.C",4,"A point that falls outside a control limit suggests:","the process may need investigation",["the process is perfect","the product is free","no action is needed"],"Out-of-control signal.")

# ---- 814 Principles of Applied Engineering II / Computer-Integrated Manufacturing II (math processes) ----
H("814.d.1.A",3,"A shop planner uses ratios and unit conversions to decide how many pallets of parts can fit in a delivery truck and how much the load will cost. She is applying mathematics to problems arising in:","everyday life, society and the workplace",["only a math contest","only a textbook example","only a game board"],"Math solves real workplace problems.")
H("814.d.1.A",4,"A manufacturer needs 540 bolts for 90 identical assemblies. The bolts per assembly is:","6",["5","9","50"],"540 ÷ 90 = 6.")
H("814.d.1.B",3,"Told that a machine makes 120 parts per hour with 5 percent scrapped, a technician first lists what is known, plans how to find the good parts, solves, and then checks whether the answer makes sense. This is a:","problem-solving model of analyzing, planning, solving and justifying",["guess-and-skip method","copy-from-a-friend method","pick-the-longest-answer method"],"Analyze, plan, solve, check.")
H("814.d.1.B",4,"A machine makes 120 parts per hour with 5 percent scrapped. How many good parts per hour?","114",["115","110","119"],"5 percent of 120 is 6, and 120 - 6 = 114.")
H("814.d.1.C",3,"To check that a bracket's hole spacing is 2.250 inches, a technician chooses a digital caliper over a tape measure and records the reading. She is selecting:","tools, including technology, and techniques to solve the problem",["the least accurate tool","a random tool","no tool"],"Tool choice affects accuracy.")
H("814.d.1.C",4,"To measure a part to the nearest thousandth of an inch, which tool is most appropriate?","a micrometer or digital caliper",["a yardstick","a tape measure","a protractor"],"Precision tools match tolerance.")
H("814.d.1.D",3,"A line lead explains to the crew, with a labeled diagram, why measuring from the same datum edge on every part prevents stacked errors. She is communicating:","mathematical ideas, reasoning and their implications using multiple representations",["only memorized rules","only a final number","only a rumor"],"Explain with words and diagrams.")
H("814.d.1.D",4,"Which representation best shows how a part's dimensions relate to each other?","a labeled dimensioned drawing",["a song lyric","a color swatch","a menu"],"Drawings show dimensional relationships.")
H("814.d.1.E",3,"A quality team records weekly defect counts in a table, plots them on a graph and writes a one-line note about the trend. They are creating and using:","representations to organize, record and communicate mathematical ideas",["random doodles","unlabeled scrap notes","only verbal guesses"],"Tables and graphs record data.")
H("814.d.1.E",4,"A line graph of defects per week is useful because it shows:","how the number changes over time",["only the largest number","only the smallest number","nothing about time"],"Line graphs show trends.")
H("814.d.1.F",3,"A planner notices that doubling the batch size doubles the material needed and sees that cost per part falls when setup cost is spread over more parts. She is analyzing:","mathematical relationships to connect and communicate mathematical ideas",["unrelated facts","only the final price","only a picture"],"Relationships between quantities.")
H("814.d.1.F",4,"If a $200 setup cost is spread evenly across 100 parts, the setup cost per part is:","$2",["$0.20","$20","$200"],"200 ÷ 100 = 2.")
H("814.d.1.G",3,"A technician posts her tolerance calculation on the board, shows each step and explains why the measured part is within limits. She is displaying, explaining and justifying:","mathematical ideas and arguments using precise mathematical language",["opinions without support","only a final answer","only a drawing"],"Justify with steps and language.")
H("814.d.1.G",4,"A part must be 5.00 inches plus or minus 0.02 inches. Which measured length is acceptable?","5.01 inches",["5.05 inches","4.95 inches","5.03 inches"],"Range is 4.98 to 5.02.")
H("814.d.2.A",3,"A student models a robotic gripper in 3D software, adds dimensions and prepares drawings for fabrication. She is using:","computer-aided design (CAD) software to complete a design",["presentation software only","a text editor only","a camera only"],"CAD creates technical designs.")
H("814.d.2.A",4,"A drawing exported from CAD for a machine shop should include:","dimensions and tolerances",["a decorative border only","only a title","only colors"],"Prints need sizes.")
H("814.d.2.B",3,"A team adjusts the wall thickness of a bracket in its model after the simulation shows deflection above the limit, then reruns the test. They are analyzing:","the results of product testing in a simulated modeling environment",["a menu","a score","a schedule"],"Simulation guides redesign.")
H("814.d.2.B",4,"If a simulation shows a part bending too much, the engineer should most likely:","change the design to make it stiffer and rerun the test",["ignore the result","skip the test","paint the part"],"Iterate on the design.")
H("814.d.2.C",3,"After the model passes simulation, a student machines a physical sample of a bearing housing to check fit on a shaft. She is:","fabricating a prototype design of a mechanical part",["printing a poster","writing a report only","drawing a cartoon"],"Prototype confirms fit.")
H("814.d.2.C",4,"Fabricating a prototype can reveal problems that:","did not show up in the computer model",["cannot exist","never matter","are always cosmetic"],"Real-world testing finds issues.")
H("814.d.2.D",3,"A class uses software to simulate a cell in which a robot loads a mill and an inspection station checks each part before packing. They are using:","computer-integrated manufacturing techniques to simulate a manufacturing process",["a game console","a music player","a calendar"],"CIM simulation previews flow.")
H("814.d.2.D",4,"Simulating a manufacturing cell before building it helps a company to:","spot bottlenecks and plan layout cheaply",["avoid all planning","skip safety","remove workers"],"Simulation finds problems early.")
H("814.d.3.A",3,"A team designs a sensor-and-relay system that stops a conveyor automatically when a box jams. They are developing:","solutions to use control devices",["a poster","a menu","a field trip"],"Control devices automate responses.")
H("814.d.3.A",4,"A system that stops a machine automatically when a sensor detects a jam is an example of:","automatic control",["manual control only","no control","random control"],"Sensors trigger actions.")
H("814.d.3.B",3,"A technician traces power to a PLC input module with a multimeter and finds that a sensor wire has come loose. He is:","troubleshooting control devices such as programmable logic circuit devices",["painting a cabinet","labeling boxes","ordering lunch"],"Trace signals to find faults.")
H("814.d.3.B",4,"The first step when troubleshooting a machine that will not start is usually to:","check for power and any tripped safety devices",["replace the whole machine","hit the machine","ignore the problem"],"Start with the simplest checks.")
H("814.d.4.A",3,"A student uses CAM software to define a part, select cutting tools and generate the code for a lathe. She is designing a project using:","computer-aided manufacturing (CAM) software for a CNC lathe",["a drawing app only","a calendar","a spreadsheet only"],"CAM generates CNC code.")
H("814.d.4.A",4,"The output of CAM software that tells a CNC machine what to do is called:","G-code",["spam","a screenshot","a calendar entry"],"G-code drives CNC machines.")
H("814.d.4.B",3,"A class checks a lathe program in a simulator, then turns a stepped aluminum shaft and measures each diameter. They are producing:","a product on a CNC lathe or simulator",["a quilt","a poem","a playlist"],"Simulate, then cut.")
H("814.d.4.B",4,"When a CNC lathe turns a stepped shaft, each step diameter is controlled by:","the program's X-axis tool positions",["the room temperature","the operator's mood","the lighting"],"X positions set diameters.")
H("814.d.4.C",3,"A team draws a flat plate with four holes and a slot in CAM software and defines the cutters and depths for a milling machine. They are designing a project using CAM for:","a CNC mill",["a sewing machine","a copier","a blender"],"Mills cut flat features.")
H("814.d.4.C",4,"For a CNC mill program, the tool's depth of cut and feed rate are chosen so that:","the cutter removes material without breaking or overheating",["the cut is as deep as possible","the tool spins slowly","the part is ignored"],"Balanced cutting parameters.")
H("814.d.4.D",3,"A student clamps a block, sets the zero point and runs the mill program, first in simulation and then on the real machine. She is producing:","a product on a CNC mill or simulator",["a mural","a video","a song"],"Run on mill after simulating.")
H("814.d.4.D",4,"The 'work zero' that a CNC mill operator sets on the stock defines:","the starting reference point for the program",["the weight of the part","the color of the cutter","the end of the program"],"Work offsets reference the program.")
H("814.d.4.E",3,"A class logs the plan, the actions taken, the inspection data and the improvements made on a shared form for each project. They are completing:","data sheets for plan, do, check and act forms and projects",["a list of snacks","a seating chart","a game score"],"PDCA forms record improvement.")
H("814.d.4.E",4,"The 'act' step of plan-do-check-act is where a team:","standardizes what worked or adjusts the plan",["ignores the results","deletes the data","stops the project"],"Act = apply learning.")
H("814.d.5.A",3,"A student builds a belt-and-pulley system, a cam-and-follower and a gear set and tests how each moves a load. She is using:","mechanical devices",["only electrical devices","only optical devices","only fluid devices"],"Mechanical devices move loads.")
H("814.d.5.A",4,"A cam and follower mechanism converts rotating motion into:","linear back-and-forth motion",["only heat","only light","only sound"],"Cams create reciprocating motion.")
H("814.d.5.B",3,"A class connects an air compressor, a regulator and a small cylinder and uses a valve to extend and retract a rod. They are using:","pneumatic devices",["hydraulic jacks only","magnets","optical sensors"],"Pneumatics use compressed air.")
H("814.d.5.B",4,"Pneumatic systems are powered by:","compressed air",["compressed oil","steam only","sunlight"],"Air power.")
H("814.d.5.C",3,"A student connects a hand pump, hoses and a hydraulic cylinder and notices the cylinder lifts a heavy block with little hand effort. They are using:","hydraulic devices",["pneumatic tools only","magnets","wind turbines"],"Hydraulics multiply force.")
H("814.d.5.C",4,"Compared with pneumatic systems, hydraulic systems can usually exert:","greater force because liquids are nearly incompressible",["less force","no force","the same weak force"],"Hydraulic fluids resist compression.")
H("814.d.6.A",3,"A student wires a start/stop station, a contactor and an overload relay to run a small motor safely. She is using:","electrical controls",["only hand tools","only fluid power","only gears"],"Controls start and protect motors.")
H("814.d.6.A",4,"An overload relay in a motor circuit is used to:","protect the motor from drawing too much current",["add speed","increase noise","reduce light"],"Overload protection.")
H("814.d.6.B",3,"A team heats samples of three plastics to different temperatures and measures how much each expands and softens. They are analyzing:","the effects of heat energy and temperature on products",["the effects of music on grades","the effects of paint on speed","the effects of snacks on sleep"],"Heat affects properties.")
H("814.d.6.B",4,"Metals generally become more ductile and may lose strength when:","heated to high temperatures",["cooled slightly","wrapped in paper","painted"],"High heat alters properties.")
H("814.d.6.C",3,"A class studies how a plant's heating, air conditioning and exhaust fans move air to keep fumes away from workers. They are developing an understanding of:","ventilation, such as heating, air conditioning and exhaust",["sports scheduling","musical rhythm","map reading"],"Ventilation controls air quality.")
H("814.d.6.C",4,"A welding shop installs exhaust hoods mainly to:","remove fumes and protect workers' lungs",["add decoration","increase noise","raise fumes"],"Local exhaust removes hazards.")
H("814.d.7.A",3,"A line tech plots the average of five measured parts every hour against control limits and flags a downward trend in time to adjust the machine. She is applying:","statistical process control",["a hunch","a rumor","a coin toss"],"SPC tracks stability.")
H("814.d.7.A",4,"An upward or downward trend of several points in a row on a control chart usually indicates:","the process may be shifting",["a perfect process","no problem","a measurement of price"],"Trends signal drift.")
H("814.d.7.B",3,"A technician presses a diamond tip into a steel sample under a set load and measures the size of the dent to find how hard the metal is. She is determining:","hardness values of different materials",["weights of different parts","colors of different metals","prices of different bolts"],"Hardness tests use indentation.")
H("814.d.7.B",4,"A Rockwell hardness test measures a material's:","resistance to indentation",["electrical resistance","color","density only"],"Rockwell = indentation hardness.")
H("814.d.7.C",3,"A bar chart counts defects by cause, and a cumulative line shows that two causes account for most defects. The team is analyzing:","attribute and Pareto charts",["a cookbook","a season schedule","a seating chart"],"Pareto charts rank causes.")
H("814.d.7.C",4,"On a Pareto chart, the bars are arranged:","from the most frequent cause to the least frequent",["alphabetically","at random","from newest to oldest"],"Descending order highlights priorities.")
H("814.d.8.A",3,"A team sketches a system in which a push button energizes a relay that opens a valve to move an air cylinder to stamp a part. They are designing a system with:","electrical controls and a pneumatic or hydraulic component",["only a pencil","only a gear set","only a spring"],"Electrical controls drive fluid power.")
H("814.d.8.A",4,"A solenoid valve in an air system is operated by:","an electrical signal",["a hand crank only","gravity only","sound"],"Solenoids convert signals to motion.")
H("814.d.8.B",3,"Following their schematic, students connect a control panel, a valve and an air cylinder and wire a start button to extend the rod. They are building:","a system that incorporates electrical controls and a pneumatic or hydraulic component",["a birdhouse","a paper airplane","a quilt"],"Build per the schematic.")
H("814.d.8.B",4,"Before powering up a newly built control system, the team should:","double-check wiring and air connections and clear the work area",["skip the check","cover the cylinder","remove safety guards"],"Verify before power-up.")
H("814.d.8.C",3,"The air cylinder does not extend when the start button is pressed, so the team checks the supply pressure, the valve coil and the wiring in turn. They are:","testing and troubleshooting the system",["abandoning the system","guessing","buying a new machine"],"Systematic troubleshooting.")
H("814.d.8.C",4,"When a system fails, a good troubleshooting approach is to:","test one section at a time to isolate the fault",["change everything at once","ignore the symptoms","blame the operator"],"Isolate the cause.")
